# A grammar whose nullable symbols appear one per round, to watch the fixed point grow:
#   round 1: A (A -> ε)
#   round 2: B (B -> A A, and A is already nullable)
#   round 3: S (S -> B B)
#   round 4: nothing new: the fixed point.
# Try it with: npm run sabueso -- nullable --grammar-file examples/grammars/nullable-chain.grammar --steps
S -> A B 'x' | B B
B -> A A | 'b'
A -> 'a' | ε
